# Copy this file to `.env` for local development:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored, but only so you don't have to re-edit a tracked file —
# not because these values are sensitive. Both variables below are PUBLIC. Vite
# inlines every `VITE_`-prefixed variable into the JavaScript bundle at build
# time, so both values are readable in the shipped site by anyone who opens
# devtools. That is fine and expected; see the Security model section of
# README.md. Never put a real secret in a VITE_ variable.
#
# In CI these same two values come from GitHub Actions repository *variables*
# (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > Variables), not secrets.

# OAuth 2.0 Client ID, type "Web application".
# Google Cloud console > APIs & Services > Credentials > Create credentials.
# Public. It is protected by its "Authorized JavaScript origins" list, which
# must contain http://localhost:5173 and https://huangwaylon.github.io — a
# client ID used from any other origin is rejected by Google.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz012345.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Browser API key, used by the Google Picker.
# Google Cloud console > APIs & Services > Credentials > Create credentials.
# Public. It is protected by an HTTP-referrer application restriction plus an
# API restriction limiting it to the Sheets, Drive, and Picker APIs.
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIzaSyDUMMY-replace-with-your-own-browser-key
